IDEAS, NO CODE
--------------
These projects shaped Hillium, but none of their code or assets is in it.
  Helium (imputnet/helium, helium-linux) — GPL-3.0: the privacy defaults Hillium
    copies at the Electron level (no Google services, built-in blocking, HTTPS first,
    DoH presets). docs/helium-parity.md lists them.
  ungoogled-chromium — BSD-3-Clause: Helium's base, and the idea of no Google traffic.
  Arc (The Browser Company) — proprietary: spaces, favourites, pinned and Today tabs,
    auto-archive, the command bar, Little Arc, Peek, Boosts and Zap, Air Traffic Control.
  alfred-browser-tabs (epilande) — MIT: fuzzy search across every open tab.
  OpenDia (aeonfun/opendia) — MIT: the browser tools offered to AI agents.
  CLI-Anything (HKUDS) — Apache-2.0: a CLI with --json output for agents.
  ArchiveBox — MIT: "archive this page" through its REST API.
  privacytests.org (privacytests/privacytests) — MIT: what to test (docs/privacy-results.md).
  Brave — MPL-2.0: the per-site shields panel and its blocked counter.
  retro-404 (gaoryrt) — no licence: an error page as a Windows 98 dialog.
  The Retro 98 look is drawn with CSS only: no Windows artwork, fonts or wallpapers.
  LGGC-liquid-glass (u7663394) — MIT and liquid-glass-effect (kevinbism) — MIT:
    compared before choosing archisvaze/liquid-glass for the glass.

